4.3 Bluetooth controller firmware patch data

  drivers/btstack-integration/bt-fw/
      LICENSE.txt   (Infineon End User License Agreement)
  drivers/btstack-integration/bt-fw/bt-fw-cywl-6208/
      btfw.hcd        Bluetooth controller patch data, HCD format
      fw_version.txt  patch version string the stack compares against
  drivers/btstack-integration/bt-fw/tools/hcd2c.py
      Aerolynq's generator: .hcd -> btfw.c at build time

      The patch data is the Infineon CYW43438 Bluetooth firmware for the
      CYWL6208 module, Generic UART 26 MHz configuration
      (wlbga_eLG_lite_AnyCloud). The embedded descriptor in the .hcd reads
      "BCM4343A1 UART 26 MHz wlbga_eLG_lite_AnyCloud" (the chip's internal
      designation; the solution is Infineon's); fw_version.txt holds
      the full version string
      "BCM4343A1_001.002.009.0153.0000_Generic_UART_26MHz_wlbga_eLG_lite_AnyCloud".
      Source: https://github.com/Infineon/bt-fw-azw-cyw43438
      (bt-fw-azw-cyw43438, version 1.0.0.2595). The .hcd is shipped complete
      and unmodified.

      This data belongs to Infineon Technologies AG (formerly Cypress
      Semiconductor Corporation, which was acquired by Infineon in 2019) and
      its suppliers, and is governed by the Infineon End User License
      Agreement reproduced as LICENSE.txt in this directory.
      That agreement permits compiling the Firmware Source Code to create
      Firmware for an Infineon hardware product, and distributing Firmware
      in binary form only, when installed on a device that includes the
      Infineon hardware product. Keep the Source Code confidential, keep the
      copyright notices, and distribute under your standard end user license
      agreement with the liability and reverse-engineering terms the EULA
      requires. Source-code redistribution beyond what the EULA allows is
      not permitted.

      The C file the stack links against (btfw.c, holding
      brcm_patch_version, brcm_patchram_format, brcm_patchram_buf and
      brcm_patch_ram_length) is NOT part of the distributed Package. It is
      generated locally at build time by tools/hcd2c.py when Bluetooth is
      enabled, from the .hcd shipped above: selecting Bluetooth in the
      configuration is enough, no extra tool or switch is needed. The
      generated file is excluded from version control and from releases
      (see .gitignore in this directory). The generator's output was
      checked byte-for-byte against Infineon's reference btfw.c: identical
      patch bytes.

  drivers/btstack-integration/bt-fw/bt-fw-cywl-6209/
  drivers/btstack-integration/bt-fw/bt-fw-cywl-6302/
  drivers/btstack-integration/bt-fw/bt-fw-cywl-6305/
  drivers/btstack-integration/bt-fw/bt-fw-cywl-6612/
      These directories are empty in this release. They hold the place for
      the patch data of the other supported Bluetooth chips: the .hcd patch
      file, its fw_version.txt, one set per chip. For each chip, obtain the
      matching Infineon bt-firmware package, check its license before
      distributing it, and place the .hcd set here together with the
      Infineon EULA text that covers it. The matching btfw.c is then
      generated automatically at build time.

      Building Bluetooth support also requires the Infineon BTStack protocol
      stack, which is not part of this Package (see Section 6).

